{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #17 (Claude Code backend) in user/delegate. Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no `delegate` runs. Follow AGENTS.md. Stay on branch `17-claude` in this worktree; do not create branches; commit on it; do not push.\n\nRead first: `gh issue view 17` and `gh issue view 17 --comments` (rulings), `gh issue view 15 --comments` (amended interface), src/backends/mod.rs, src/backends/cursor/mod.rs, src/backends/types.rs, src/stream.rs, src/models.rs, src/cli_info.rs, src/finalize.rs, tests/cli_e2e.rs, tests/live.rs, and the fixtures in tests/fixtures/claude/ (*.stdout and *.argv).\n\nREQUIRED behaviour:\n1. New enum variant, exactly: `Claude,` in `pub enum Backend` (src/backends/mod.rs), with `from_name(\"claude\") => Some(Self::Claude)`, `name() => \"claude\"`, and a match arm in every method. New module src/backends/claude/ (mod.rs, plus doctor if separate).\n2. Binary: `CLAUDE_BIN` env override, then `which claude`, then `~/.local/bin/claude` (mirror cursor's resolve_bin).\n3. argv (without the binary). Read-only (Capability::Ask), new session — literally:\n   `-p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model claude-sonnet-5-5 --permission-mode plan --session-id <uuid> -- <prompt>`\n   Read-write (Capability::WriteUnsandboxed), new session:\n   `-p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model claude-sonnet-5-5 --permission-mode auto --session-id <uuid> -- <prompt>`\n   Resume (session Some(id)): replace `--session-id <uuid>` with `--resume <id>`.\n   The new-session uuid comes from `crate::util::random_uuid()` inside argv. is_write = capability is WriteUnsandboxed. Plan mode only for read-only: no --disallowedTools fallback.\n4. Parser: extend the shared stream parser (src/stream.rs / cursor finish) rather than copying it. Claude lines: skip `system/*` (hook_started, hook_response, init, commands_changed) and `rate_limit_event`; progress from `assistant` message content items of type `tool_use` (tool name; path from input.file_path/path) and `text`; `result` line: `result` text, `session_id`, `is_error` (authoritative over `subtype`), `duration_ms`, `total_cost_usd` → BackendResult.cost_usd (so cost_estimated=false), usage snake_case: input_tokens→inputTokens, output_tokens→outputTokens, cache_read_input_tokens→cacheReadTokens, cache_creation_input_tokens→cacheWriteTokens. Clean exit without a result line → ERROR (same as cursor). CANCELLED is never the parser's.\n   Expected normalized result for tests/fixtures/claude/plan-plain-answer.stdout (clean exit):\n   BackendResult { text: \"391\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE\", session_id: Some(\"25dddfc3-4271-4019-9de0-6795bd6483fa\"), usage: Some(Usage { input_tokens: 2.0, output_tokens: 12.0, cache_read_tokens: 10261.0, cache_write_tokens: 16891.0 }), cost_usd: Some(0.0697402), is_error: Some(false), duration_ms: Some(2245.0), clean_exit: true, stderr: \"\" }\n5. permission_denials: when the result line's `permission_denials` array is non-empty, the job ends DONE_WITH_CONCERNS (unless already ERROR) with a concern listing the denied tool names, and the denials are kept in a record field. Test with a minimal synthetic result line in a unit test, labelled `// synthetic: no refusal was recorded in #6`.\n6. Errors: tests/fixtures/claude/error-bad-model.stdout (exit 1, result line is_error true, subtype \"success\") → ERROR with the result text.\n7. Doctor: claude section — binary found, `claude --version`, login via `claude auth status` (JSON, `loggedIn` true = ok, false = fail). Remove claude from the \"backend not implemented\" skip list / resolve_model stub (src/models.rs, src/cli_info.rs) — pi stays unimplemented. Update the tests that asserted the claude stub.\n8. Tests:\n   - Parser test per claude fixture on origin/main (tests/fixtures/claude/*.stdout): plan-plain-answer, plan-review, plan-edit-request (NEEDS_CONTEXT text), auto-fix (tool calls), auto-refusal*, resume-answer, needs-context, error-bad-model, cancelled (no result line → ERROR from the parser; supervisor owns CANCELLED).\n   - e2e (tests/cli_e2e.rs or a new tests/claude_e2e.rs): a fake `claude` shell script selected by CLAUDE_BIN that `cat`s a fixture (copied into the test temp dir) and exits with the recorded code; cover run+watch, resume (assert argv got `--resume <id>` — have the fake append its argv to a file), cancel (fake waits on a release file, never sleep), and read-only argv has `--permission-mode plan`. Fakes wait on release files, never sleeps.\n   - tests/live.rs: add an `#[ignore]` claude round trip (claude-sonnet-5-5, read-only, \"What is 17 * 23?\"); it writes the raw stdout through `jq -rR -L scripts 'include \"redact\"; (fromjson? | redact | tojson) // .'` to tests/fixtures/claude/live-plain-answer.stdout. Do not run it.\n9. skills/delegate/SKILL.md: make claude models runnable (edit the \"Only cursor models run today\" sentence and the Model picks row), and add one line: plan mode's blocking of a writing Bash command is untested (#6), so don't rely on read-only Claude for anything a shell write could damage. Nothing else in the skill.\n\nFence: owns src/backends/ (claude module, enum arms, shared parser), src/stream.rs, src/doctor.rs, src/cli_info.rs and src/models.rs (only the claude stub/skip removal), src/finalize.rs or src/types.rs only if the permission_denials field/concern needs it (list it in your report), tests/, skills/delegate/SKILL.md (item 9 only). Forbidden: pi backend work, .github/, scripts/, tests/fixtures/ contents (read-only; copy into temp dirs in tests), anything outside this worktree.\n\nGate before committing: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` (all green, including tests/budgets.rs). Commit with a conventional message ending `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>`.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA and the test summary (passed/failed counts), or a failure triage — nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"a6874d86-60bb-4e84-8f2b-a3973591ec9a"}
