3\nfc_19bac0a1-6fdb-9d76-bd66-a5e00e5f2561_3","startedAtMs":"1790855482217"},"model_call_id":"a6d3412c-3430-4550-9d20-13547e35e0bc-0-6eqz","session_id":"a6874d86-60bb-4e84-8f2b-a3973591ec9a","timestamp_ms":1790855482107}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-5d6069e3-24eb-479f-8020-a40449666b25-3\nfc_19bac0a1-6fdb-9d76-bd66-a5e00e5f2561_3","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"gh issue view 17 && echo \"===== COMMENTS =====\" && gh issue view 17 --comments && echo \"===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\" && gh issue view 15 --comments","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-5d6069e3-24eb-479f-8020-a40449666b25-3\nfc_19bac0a1-6fdb-9d76-bd66-a5e00e5f2561_3","simpleCommands":["gh","echo","gh","echo","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"17"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 17"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"===== COMMENTS =====\""}],"fullText":"echo \"===== COMMENTS =====\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"17"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 17 --comments"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\""}],"fullText":"echo \"===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"15"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 15 --comments"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch issues 17 and 15 with comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"a6874d86-60bb-4e84-8f2b-a3973591ec9a","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"a6d3412c-3430-4550-9d20-13547e35e0bc"},"result":{"success":{"command":"gh issue view 17 && echo \"===== COMMENTS =====\" && gh issue view 17 --comments && echo \"===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\" && gh issue view 15 --comments","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"title:\tClaude backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t17\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n===== COMMENTS =====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Read-only:** `--permission-mode plan` only. Per the #6 probe there is no `--disallowedTools` fallback; strike that wording from the ticket. Whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command is still untested; record that as a known risk in the skill (#14).\n2. **Fake binary:** `CLAUDE_BIN` overrides the binary. The e2e fake replays a recorded NDJSON fixture.\n3. **Session:** the run generates a UUID and passes `--session-id`; resume passes `--resume <id>`.\n4. **Parser:** extend the shared cursor parser rather than copying it. Claude needs to:\n   - skip `system/hook_*`, `commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event`\n   - read progress from `tool_use`/`tool_result`\n   - read `total_cost_usd` from the `result` line and report it as the job's cost\n   - map snake_case usage fields\n   - treat `is_error` as authoritative over `subtype`\n5. **Permission denials:** a non-empty `permission_denials` makes the run DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, with the denials listed and kept in a record field. No refusal was recorded in #6, so use a minimal synthetic `result` line in a unit test and label it synthetic.\n6. **Missing result line:** a clean exit with no `result` line is ERROR.\n7. **Doctor:** the login probe is `claude auth status` (JSON with `loggedIn`). Delete #11's stub for claude.\n8. **Live test:** the opt-in live test pipes its fixture through `scripts/redact.jq`.\n--\n===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Interface:** an enum `Backend { Cursor }` (pi and claude variants arrive in #16 and #17), with `match` in each method. No `dyn` trait: three closed variants don't need one. Its methods are `bin`, `argv(model, capability, cwd, session)`, `parse` (stream to a normalized result: text, session id, usage, optional cost, error), `resume_args`, and doctor probes. The CLI `doctor` command stays where #11 put it and calls the probes.\n2. **Encapsulation:** `build_argv`, the capability-to-flag mapping and the cursor binary resolution move into `backends/cursor`. Delete the non-spec capability modes if #13 left any.\n3. **Parsers:** `stream.rs` stays at the crate root, so the #17 Claude parser can reuse it. STATUS-line parsing stays outside the backend, in `output.rs`.\n4. **Fixture tests:** one test for each `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout`. Keep the existing inline tests.\n5. **Failure cases:**\n   - A bad model (empty stdout, exit 1) is an error built from the exit code and stderr.\n   - Lines that don't parse are skipped.\n   - A clean exit with no `result` line is ERROR.\n   - CANCELLED is set by the supervisor, never the parser.\n6. **Behaviour:** unchanged. Existing tests may change their imports only.\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nAmendment to ruling 1 (orchestrator): the interface as landed in #29 is `from_name`, `name`, `bin`, `argv(model, capability, session, prompt)` (resume flags are built inside `argv`), and `spawn`. #16 and #17 add a `parse` match arm when a second parser exists. `cwd` reaches the child through `JobSpec.cwd`.\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":4175,"interleavedOutput":"title:\tClaude backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t17\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n===== COMMENTS =====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Read-only:** `--permission-mode plan` only. Per the #6 probe there is no `--disallowedTools` fallback; strike that wording from the ticket. Whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command is still untested; record that as a known risk in the skill (#14).\n2. **Fake binary:** `CLAUDE_BIN` overrides the binary. The e2e fake replays a recorded NDJSON fixture.\n3. **Session:** the run generates a UUID and passes `--session-id`; resume passes `--resume <id>`.\n4. **Parser:** extend the shared cursor parser rather than copying it. Claude needs to:\n   - skip `system/hook_*`, `commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event`\n   - read progress from `tool_use`/`tool_result`\n   - read `total_cost_usd` from the `result` line and report it as the job's cost\n   - map snake_case usage fields\n   - treat `is_error` as authoritative over `subtype`\n5. **Permission denials:** a non-empty `permission_denials` makes the run DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, with the denials listed and kept in a record field. No refusal was recorded in #6, so use a minimal synthetic `result` line in a unit test and label it synthetic.\n6. **Missing result line:** a clean exit with no `result` line is ERROR.\n7. **Doctor:** the login probe is `claude auth status` (JSON with `loggedIn`). Delete #11's stub for claude.\n8. **Live test:** the opt-in live test pipes its fixture through `scripts/redact.jq`.\n--\n===== ISSUE 15 COMMENTS =====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Interface:** an enum `Backend { Cursor }` (pi and claude variants arrive in #16 and #17), with `match` in each method. No `dyn` trait: three closed variants don't need one. Its methods are `bin`, `argv(model, capability, cwd, session)`, `parse` (stream to a normalized result: text, session id, usage, optional cost, error), `resume_args`, and doctor probes. The CLI `doctor` command stays where #11 put it and calls the probes.\n2. **Encapsulation:** `build_argv`, the capability-to-flag mapping and the cursor binary resolution move into `backends/cursor`. Delete the non-spec capability modes if #13 left any.\n3. **Parsers:** `stream.rs` stays at the crate root, so the #17 Claude parser can reuse it. STATUS-line parsing stays outside the backend, in `output.rs`.\n4. **Fixture tests:** one test for each `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout`. Keep the existing inline tests.\n5. **Failure cases:**\n   - A bad model (empty stdout, exit 1) is an error built from the exit code and stderr.\n   - Lines that don't parse are skipped.\n   - A clean exit with no `result` line is ERROR.\n   - CANCELLED is set by the supervisor, never the parser.\n6. **Behaviour:** unchanged. Existing tests may change their imports only.\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nAmendment to ruling 1 (orchestrator): the interface as landed in #29 is `from_name`, `name`, `bin`, `argv(model, capability, session, prompt)` (resume flags are built inside `argv`), and `spawn`. #16 and #17 add a `parse` match arm when a second parser exists. `cwd` reaches the child through `JobSpec.cwd`.\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":3693},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch issues 17 and 15 with comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-5d6069e3-24eb-479f-8020-a40449666b25-3\nfc_19bac0a1-6fdb-9d76-bd66-a5e00e5f2561_3","startedAtMs":"1790855482217","completedAtMs":"1790855486551"},"model_call_id":"a6d3412c-3430-4550-9d20-13547e35e0bc-0-6eqz","session_id":"a6874d86-60bb-4e84-8f2b-a3973591ec9a","timestamp_ms":1790855486449}
